    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your companion is an oversized worm covered in knobby growths, used by goblinoid farmers to till soil and eat pests.</p><p><strong>Size</strong> Small</p><p><strong>Melee</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> body, Damage 1d8 bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Melee</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> jaws (agile), Damage 1d6 slashing</p><p><strong>Str</strong> +3, <strong>Dex</strong> +1, <strong>Con</strong> +2, <strong>Int</strong> –4, <strong>Wis</strong> +1, <strong>Cha</strong> +1</p><p><strong>Hit Points</strong> 8</p><p><strong>Skill</strong> Survival</p><p><strong>Speed</strong> 20 feet</p><p><strong>Support Benefit</strong> Your knurled worm secretes a slippery slime. Until the start of your next turn, if you hit and deal damage to a creature within your knurled worm's reach, the first square the creature moves into after taking that damage is difficult terrain.</p><p><strong>Advanced Maneuver</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.sf-AC-Advanced-Maneuvers.Item.sbPPiJz5cOMts1dO]{Regurgitate Soil}</p>",
